@page "/privacy"
@layout AuthLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy — AI Labs</PageTitle>

<div class="legal-doc-page">
    <h1 class="legal-doc-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-doc-meta">Last modified: November 25, 2026</p>
    <p class="legal-doc-meta">Effective Date: November 25, 2026</p>

    <h2 class="legal-doc-h2">Summary of Changes</h2>
    <p class="legal-doc-p">
        We have revised this Privacy Policy. This summary is intended to briefly explain how AI Labs collects, uses, and protects your information. We encourage you to review the full Privacy Policy below. Key highlights include:
    </p>
    <ul class="legal-doc-ul">
        <li>clarification on zero model training using customer prompts, code, or inference outputs without explicit consent;</li>
        <li>streamlined alignment with our <a href="/terms" class="legal-doc-link">Terms of Service</a>; and</li>
        <li>updated details on encryption standards and user data deletion rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="legal-doc-hr" />

    <section class="legal-doc-section">
        <h3 class="legal-doc-h3">1. Information We Collect</h3>
        <p class="legal-doc-p">
            We collect minimal information necessary to deliver and secure our cloud services:
        </p>
        <ul class="legal-doc-ul">
            <li><strong>Account Data:</strong> Name, username, encrypted password hash, and organization name.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage Telemetry:</strong> API execution timestamps, model invocation latency, token counts, and error rates to monitor platform reliability.</li>
            <li><strong>Device &amp; Session Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, operating system, and security tokens for fraud prevention.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-doc-section">
        <h3 class="legal-doc-h3">2. How We Protect Your Data</h3>
        <p class="legal-doc-p">
            Security is built into our foundational infrastructure. All data transmitted between your browser, APIs, and model endpoints is encrypted via TLS 1.3, and stored database records use AES-256 bit encryption. AI Labs does not use your proprietary code, prompts, embeddings, or inference outputs to train foundational models without your express opt-in consent.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-doc-section">
        <h3 class="legal-doc-h3">3. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h3>
        <p class="legal-doc-p">
            You hold full control over your stored records. You may request complete deletion of your account and associated project workspaces at any time through your account preferences or by contacting our Data Protection Officer.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-doc-section">
        <h3 class="legal-doc-h3">4. Compliance &amp; Your Legal Rights</h3>
        <p class="legal-doc-p">
            We adhere to international privacy frameworks including GDPR, CCPA, and applicable PDP (Pelindungan Data Pribadi) standards. You have the right to access, rectify, export, or erase your personal data at any time.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="legal-doc-footer">
        <a href="/" class="legal-doc-link">&larr; Back to Sign In</a>
    </div>
</div>
